<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 23rd century BCE</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 2200s BCE: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/23rd-century-bce">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 2250 BCE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 8238 4336" role="img" aria-label="Map: 4 numbered states of the world in 2250 BCE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="6129" cy="1232" r="140"/><text x="6129" y="1291" font-size="168">1</text></g><g><circle cx="5821" cy="1708" r="140"/><text x="5821" y="1766" font-size="168">2</text></g><g><circle cx="2866" cy="2840" r="140"/><text x="2866" y="2899" font-size="168">3</text></g><g><circle cx="6325" cy="2079" r="140"/><text x="6325" y="2138" font-size="168">4</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 2250 BCE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Land of Punt &middot; Caral-Supe &middot; Akkadian Empire &middot; Kerma</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Akkadian language</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Obelisk</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 2200s BCE, 1 recorded states were founded and 1 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Akkadian Empire, the Elamite Confederation and the Byblos. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 23rd century BCE, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/23rd-century-bce. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 23rd century BCE</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Akkadian Empire <span>2334 BCE – 2154 BCE</span></li><li>Kerma <span>2500 BCE – 1500 BCE</span></li><li>Caral-Supe <span>3000 BCE – 1800 BCE</span></li><li>Land of Punt <span>2500 BCE – 1100 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Akkadian language</dt><dd>Akkadian is an extinct Semitic language of ancient Mesopotamia, written in cuneiform.</dd><dt>Obelisk</dt><dd>An obelisk is a tall, narrow, tapering stone monument, often carved from a single block.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
